[{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Find the shortest distance from the origin to the plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+2y+9z=344\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The plane has normal vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,2,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from the origin is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\lambda(1,2,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"86\\lambda=344\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,8,36)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus the distance is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{4^2+8^2+36^2}=4\\sqrt{86}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, the point-to-plane formula gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{|344|}{\\sqrt{1^2+2^2+9^2}}=4\\sqrt{86}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Find the shortest distance between the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,1,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+y+z=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=(2,1,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(2,1,2)+\\lambda(1,1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+y+z=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\lambda+5=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-\\frac23\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac43,\\frac13,\\frac43)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{(-\\tfrac23)^2+(-\\tfrac23)^2+(-\\tfrac23)^2}=\\frac{2\\sqrt3}{3}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{|2+1+2-3|}{\\sqrt3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt3}{3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Find the shortest distance from the given point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the given plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(10,3,1),\\quad \\Pi:x-y-z=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(-3,2,8),\\quad \\Pi:2x+5y-8z=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(-9,0,60),\\quad \\Pi:-5x-3y+9z=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(6,6,-1),\\quad \\Pi:-y-2z=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-1,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.  The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(10,3,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(10,3,1)+\\lambda(1,-1,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\lambda+3=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9,4,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{(-1)^2+1^2+1^2}=\\sqrt3\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{|10-3-1-3|}{\\sqrt3}=\\sqrt3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,5,-8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(-3,2,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(-3,2,8)+\\lambda(2,5,-8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"93\\lambda-66=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=\\frac{22}{31}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac{49}{31},\\frac{172}{31},\\frac{72}{31})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{66}{\\sqrt{93}}=\\frac{22\\sqrt{93}}{31}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-5,-3,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(-9,0,60)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(-9,0,60)+\\lambda(-5,-3,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"115\\lambda+575=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(16,15,15)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{25^2+15^2+(-45)^2}=5\\sqrt{115}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{575}{\\sqrt{115}}=5\\sqrt{115}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-1,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(6,6,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(6,6,-1)+\\lambda(0,-1,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5\\lambda-5=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,5,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{0^2+(-1)^2+(-2)^2}=\\sqrt5\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{|0-6+2-1|}{\\sqrt5}=\\sqrt5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>It is given that the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has position vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-10\\mathbf i+20\\mathbf j-50\\mathbf k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the exact distance from the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x+y-15z=1698\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,1,-15)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=(-10,20,-50)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(-10,20,-50)+\\lambda(4,1,-15)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"242\\lambda-968=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(6,24,-110)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{16^2+4^2+(-60)^2}=44\\sqrt2\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{968}{\\sqrt{242}}=44\\sqrt2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>It is given that the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have equations:</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"l_1:\\ \\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\5\\\\-10\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}30\\\\1\\\\5\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad l_2:\\ \\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}20\\\\5\\\\10\\end{pmatrix}+\\mu\\begin{pmatrix}-80\\\\-3\\\\5\\end{pmatrix},\\qquad \\Pi:x-2y+3z-218=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>The coordinates of where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> intersect is point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the coordinates of point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the shortest distance of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\" data-display=\"false\"></span> from the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Equating coordinates of the two lines gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"30\\lambda+80\\mu=10,\\qquad \\lambda+3\\mu=0,\\qquad5\\lambda-5\\mu=20.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>The first two equations give <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, which satisfy the third. Substitution into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(100,8,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,-2,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(100,8,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"|1(100)-2(8)+3(5)-218|=119,\\qquad |(1,-2,3)|=\\sqrt{14}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Thus the shortest distance is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{119}{\\sqrt{14}}=\\frac{17\\sqrt{14}}2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>It is given that the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x-2y-14z+39=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and that the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}5\\\\28\\\\18\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\5\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on the line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that the shortest distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{209}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units. Find the possible coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-2,-14)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and a point on the line has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5+3\\lambda,28+5\\lambda,18+\\lambda)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The distance condition gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{|3(5+3\\lambda)-2(28+5\\lambda)-14(18+\\lambda)+39|}{\\sqrt{209}}=\\sqrt{209},\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|-254-15\\lambda|=209\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-\\frac{463}{15}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The corresponding points are</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"Q=(-4,13,15)\\quad\\text{or}\\quad Q=\\left(-\\frac{438}{5},-\\frac{379}{3},-\\frac{193}{15}\\right).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, the line through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> perpendicular to the plane has direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-2,-14)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution into the plane gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mu=(254+15\\lambda)/209\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Setting the squared distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and its foot equal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"209\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"15\\lambda^2+508\\lambda+1389=0=(\\lambda+3)(15\\lambda+463),\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>which gives the same two points.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>A large flat area of open ground is modelled as a plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"z=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. A slope mine is dug due to a coal bed, which can be modelled as a plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\1\\\\50\\end{pmatrix}=-4935\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where measurements are in metres. The entrance to the slope mine has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(25,25,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, relative to a fixed origin.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the shortest distance between the entrance to the slope mine and the coal bed.</p></li></ol><p>Due to the shortest distance being a route that was too steep, it is instead decided to reach the coal bed via a tunnel that can be modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}25\\\\25\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\11/7\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>Find the distance from the tunnel entrance to where the tunnel meets the coal bed.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The coal-bed plane has normal <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,1,50)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(25,25,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(25,25,0)+\\lambda(2,1,50)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution into the plane gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2505\\lambda+5010=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(21,23,-100)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The shortest distance is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(-4)^2+(-2)^2+(-100)^2}=2\\sqrt{2505}\\text{ m}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{5010}{\\sqrt{2505}}=2\\sqrt{2505}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Substitute the tunnel equation into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x+y+50z=-4935\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2(25+10\\lambda)+\\left(25+\\frac{11}{7}\\lambda\\right)+50\\lambda=-4935,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{501}{7}\\lambda+5010=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-70\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The tunnel meets the coal bed at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-675,-85,-70)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The distance from the entrance is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(-700)^2+(-110)^2+(-70)^2}=130\\sqrt{30}\\text{ m}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>It is given that the points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\" data-display=\"false\"></span> have coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,-1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,-2,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,2,-2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> respectively. It is also given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the acute angle between the lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BA\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BC\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies in the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the equation of the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,1,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> does not lie in the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the shortest distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Hence find the exact volume of the tetrahedron <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABCD\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, given that the volume is equal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac13\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> area of base <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\times\" data-display=\"false\"></span> perpendicular distance from base to apex.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\overrightarrow{BA}=(2,1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\overrightarrow{BC}=(2,4,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\cos\\theta=\\frac{(2,1,1)\\cdot(2,4,-1)}{\\sqrt6\\sqrt{21}}=\\frac7{\\sqrt{126}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{14}}6,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>and since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is acute, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta=\\sqrt{1-\\frac{14}{36}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>A normal to the plane is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2,1,1)\\times(2,4,-1)=(-5,4,6).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=(2,-1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5x+4y+6z=-14\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Substituting <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D=(3,1,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-5(3)+4(1)+6(5)=19\\ne-14\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not on the plane.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"D\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-5,4,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The foot occurs at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-\\frac37\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(3,1,5)+\\lambda(-5,4,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, giving <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac{36}{7},-\\frac57,\\frac{17}{7})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{33}{\\sqrt{77}}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{77}}7\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{|19-(-14)|}{\\sqrt{77}}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{77}}7\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p>The area of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac12|\\overrightarrow{BA}\\times\\overrightarrow{BC}|=\\frac12\\sqrt{(-5)^2+4^2+6^2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{77}}2.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Hence the tetrahedron volume is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac13\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{77}}2\\cdot\\frac{3\\sqrt{77}}7=\\frac{11}{2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units<span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q9","number":9,"question":"<ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the shortest distance from the origin to the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\3\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show that the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-13,4,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Write the equation of the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\hat{\\mathbf n}=d\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\hat{\\mathbf n}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the unit vector in the direction of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\begin{pmatrix}1\\\\3\\\\2\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,3,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the perpendicular from the origin meets the plane at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda(1,3,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"14\\lambda=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, and the distance is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac5{14}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{15}{14}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac57\\right)^2}=\\frac5{\\sqrt{14}}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{14}}{14}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, this is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{|5|}{\\sqrt{14}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>Substitution of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=(-13,4,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-13+3(4)+2(3)=-13+12+6=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> lies on the plane.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The unit normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\hat{\\mathbf n}=\\frac1{\\sqrt{14}}(1,3,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac5{\\sqrt{14}}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{14}}{14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\hat{\\mathbf n}=\\frac{5\\sqrt{14}}{14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>Jake is trying to find the shortest distance from the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,-3,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\4\\\\5\\end{pmatrix}=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. First, Jake finds the equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the plane that is parallel to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and contains <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the equation of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\hat{\\mathbf n}=d\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\hat{\\mathbf n}=d\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Show how Jake can use his two answers from part (b) to find the shortest distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The unit normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\hat{\\mathbf n}=\\frac1{3\\sqrt5}(-2,4,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=(2,-3,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"A\\cdot(-2,4,5)=-4-12+20=4,\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2:\\mathbf r\\cdot\\hat{\\mathbf n}=\\frac4{3\\sqrt5}=\\frac{4\\sqrt5}{15}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the constant is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac8{3\\sqrt5}=\\frac{8\\sqrt5}{15}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1:\\mathbf r\\cdot\\hat{\\mathbf n}=\\frac{8\\sqrt5}{15},\\qquad \\Pi_2:\\mathbf r\\cdot\\hat{\\mathbf n}=\\frac{4\\sqrt5}{15}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Both constants are positive, so the planes lie on the same side of the origin. Their separation, and hence the distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{8\\sqrt5}{15}-\\frac{4\\sqrt5}{15}=\\frac{4\\sqrt5}{15}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>Find the shortest distance between the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A(2,-10,-642)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\9\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The plane normal is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,9,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. A perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A=(2,-10,-642)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> meets the plane when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"91\\lambda-728=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=8\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(26,62,-634)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{24^2+72^2+8^2}=8\\sqrt{91}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{|3(2)+9(-10)-642-2|}{\\sqrt{91}}=\\frac{728}{\\sqrt{91}}=8\\sqrt{91}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units. A parallel-plane method gives the same distance: the plane through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> parallel to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has normalized constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-726/\\sqrt{91}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, while <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2/\\sqrt{91}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so their separation is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"728/\\sqrt{91}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Find the shortest distance from the origin to the plane with equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}10\\\\66\\\\-8\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\5\\\\7\\end{pmatrix}+\\mu\\begin{pmatrix}-2\\\\3\\\\9\\end{pmatrix}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>The direction vectors of the plane are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,5,7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,3,9)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. A normal is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(3,5,7)\\times(-2,3,9)=(24,-41,19).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(10,66,-8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives the plane equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"24x-41y+19z+2618=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from the origin meets it at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda(24,-41,19)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2618\\lambda+2618=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the foot is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-24,41,-19)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{24^2+41^2+19^2}=\\sqrt{2618}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{2618}{\\sqrt{2618}}=\\sqrt{2618}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>Find the shortest distance from the point with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,1,7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the plane with equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}120\\\\-15\\\\985\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\-5\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}+\\mu\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\1\\\\3\\end{pmatrix}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>A normal to the plane is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(2,-5,1)\\times(-1,1,3)=(-16,-7,-3).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Substituting <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(120,-15,985)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives the plane equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"16x+7y+3z-4770=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,1,7)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> meets the plane at parameter <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> along direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(16,7,3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(242,106,52)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{240^2+105^2+45^2}=15\\sqrt{314}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{4710}{\\sqrt{314}}=15\\sqrt{314}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>The plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span> contains both the point with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,3,-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the line with equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\4\\\\1\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}-1\\\\2\\\\4\\end{pmatrix}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Find the shortest distance from the origin to the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The two direction vectors in the plane are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-1,2,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1,6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Their cross product is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(8,6,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the plane has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"8x+6y-z-39=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, using <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,4,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The perpendicular from the origin meets the plane at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda(8,6,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"101\\lambda-39=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{39}{\\sqrt{101}}=\\frac{39\\sqrt{101}}{101}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q15","number":15,"question":"<p>Find the distance between the parallel planes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+y+z=40\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+y+z=60\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The planes have the same normal vector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The distance is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{|60-40|}{\\sqrt3}=\\frac{20\\sqrt3}{3}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>An artist is designing a sculpture made from several parallel pieces of acrylic. Two of the acrylic pieces can be modelled by the planes given by</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1:px+2y+qz=300,\\qquad \\Pi_2:px+2y+qz=627.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>It is given that the acrylic piece modelled by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> must pass through the points with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(100,-150,-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(150,-100,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the distance between the planes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>Substitution of the two points into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"px+2y+qz=300\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"100p-4q=600,\\qquad150p+10q=500.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Solving gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"q=-25\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The normals are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(5,2,-25)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The plane constants in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5x+2y-25z+d=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=-627\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=-300\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Thus</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d(\\Pi_1,\\Pi_2)=\\frac{327}{\\sqrt{654}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{654}}2\\text{ m}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q17","number":17,"question":"<p>The planes <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> are parallel. Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+2y+2z=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and that the distance between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is 5 units, find the two possible equations of plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>A normal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,2,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, of length 3. A perpendicular displacement of length 5 is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\pm\\frac53(1,2,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Starting from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives points <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac53,\\frac{10}3,\\frac{25}3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-\\frac53,-\\frac{10}3,\\frac53)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution gives the two possibilities</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Pi_2:x+2y+2z-25=0\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\Pi_2:x+2y+2z+5=0.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, applying the point-plane distance formula to a parallel plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x+2y+2z+d=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> through <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"|10+d|/3=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=-25\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>A laser is set up between two large parallel mirrors where distances are in metres. Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, the mirrors can be modelled by the equations</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1:px+9y+3z=6,\\qquad \\Pi_2:px+9y+3z=26.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>When fired, the laser passes through the points with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,10,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The laser first hits <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, making an acute angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\theta\" data-display=\"false\"></span> with the normal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span> such that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin\\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt6}{3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the coordinates of where the laser first hits <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\Pi_1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>Find the distance between the two mirrors.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>The line direction from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,2,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,10,8)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is proportional to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The angle condition gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{p^2+90}\\sqrt2}=\\frac{\\sqrt3}{3},\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p^2=126\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"p=3\\sqrt{14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>The laser has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(4,2,0)+\\lambda(0,1,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Substitution into <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3\\sqrt{14}x+9y+3z=6\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-1-\\sqrt{14}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the first point of contact is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(4,1-\\sqrt{14},-1-\\sqrt{14})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>The plane normal has length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{(3\\sqrt{14})^2+9^2+3^2}=6\\sqrt6\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The distance between the planes is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{|26-6|}{6\\sqrt6}=\\frac{5\\sqrt6}{9}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>Find the distance between the line with equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}2\\\\8\\\\-1\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\2\\\\5\\end{pmatrix}\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>and the plane with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-31x+14y+13z+2615=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The line direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,2,5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is perpendicular to the plane normal <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-31,14,13)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> because their dot product is zero. The line is not contained in the plane: its point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2,8,-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-31(2)+14(8)+13(-1)+2615=2652\\ne0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. A perpendicular from this point meets the plane at parameter <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(64,-20,-27)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Hence</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"d=\\sqrt{62^2+(-28)^2+(-26)^2}=2\\sqrt{1326}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{2652}{\\sqrt{1326}}=2\\sqrt{1326}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>Find the distance between the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x=\\frac{y-3}{2}=\\frac{60-6z}{13}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the plane with equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r\\cdot\\begin{pmatrix}3\\\\-4\\\\-3\\end{pmatrix}=60.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>The line can be written <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=(0,3,10)+\\lambda(\\frac12,2,-\\frac{13}{6})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Its direction is perpendicular to the plane normal <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-4,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so the line is parallel to the plane. The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,3,10)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is not on the plane. The perpendicular from it has direction <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3,-4,-3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and meets the plane at parameter <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\lambda=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(9,-9,1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. The distance is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\sqrt{9^2+(-12)^2+(-9)^2}=3\\sqrt{34}\\text{ units}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Alternatively, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"d=\\frac{102}{\\sqrt{34}}=3\\sqrt{34}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> units.</p>"]},{"id":"fm-core1-1.63-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>It is given that the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(2,1,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the same distance from the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x+y+8z=-65\" data-display=\"false\"></span> as it is from the line</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathbf r=\\begin{pmatrix}0\\\\-13\\\\0\\end{pmatrix}+\\lambda\\begin{pmatrix}4\\\\3\\\\k\\end{pmatrix}.\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","steps":["<p>The distance from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P=(2,1,2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> to the plane <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x+y+8z+65=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{|8+1+16+65|}{\\sqrt{4^2+1^2+8^2}}=10.\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf a=(0,-13,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathbf d=(4,3,k)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> describe the line. Equating the point-to-line distance to 10 gives</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{|\\mathbf d\\times(P-a)|}{|\\mathbf d|}=10,\\qquad P-a=(2,14,2),\\qquad \\mathbf d\\times(P-a)=(6-14k,2k-8,50).\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Squaring and simplifying gives <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1=\\frac{2k^2-2k+26}{25+k^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(k-1)^2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]}]